<div role="alert" class="mb-5 rounded-2xl border border-amber-300 bg-amber-50 p-4 text-sm leading-6 text-amber-950">
    <strong>Draft — not an approved institutional policy.</strong>
    PIT’s Data Protection Officer contact, approved retention schedule, and final privacy procedures must be confirmed before this information is treated as official.
</div>

<article class="space-y-6 rounded-3xl bg-white p-5 text-sm leading-7 text-slate-700 shadow-sm ring-1 ring-slate-200 sm:p-8">
    <section>
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900">Information this system handles</h3>
        <p class="mt-2">The system may process account and contact details, organization or department information, reservation schedules, requested venues and equipment, supporting documents, electronic signatures, approval actions, notifications, and related activity history. The fields requested may vary by account type and form.</p>
    </section>
    <section>
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900">Why the information is used</h3>
        <p class="mt-2">Information is used to create and manage accounts, check availability, evaluate and approve requests, coordinate equipment, communicate status changes, maintain request history, and protect the service from misuse. The institution must confirm any additional purposes before publication.</p>
    </section>
    <section>
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900">Who may access it</h3>
        <p class="mt-2">Access is intended to be limited by account role and assigned responsibility. Requestors can view their own requests; assigned custodians can review relevant requests; and authorized administrators can perform system administration and final review. Public calendar information is limited and does not show private requestor contact details.</p>
    </section>
    <section>
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900">Documents and electronic signatures</h3>
        <p class="mt-2">Supporting documents and signatures may contain personal information. They are intended for authorized request and approval workflows and should not be shared outside those purposes. Do not upload information that is not needed for your request.</p>
    </section>
    <section>
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900">Storage and retention</h3>
        <p class="mt-2">The production hosting location, backup schedule, retention period, and secure-disposal procedures must be confirmed by PIT.</p>
        <p class="mt-2 rounded-xl bg-slate-50 p-3"><strong>To be completed by PIT:</strong> Identify the approved records-retention schedule, storage location, backup controls, and deletion or archival process.</p>
    </section>
    <section>
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900">Your privacy questions and requests</h3>
        <p class="mt-2">The Data Privacy Act of 2012 provides rights and protections for personal information, subject to the law’s conditions and exceptions. PIT has not provided an official privacy contact or process for questions and requests. Confirm the appropriate contact channel with the institution.</p>
    </section>
    <p class="border-t border-slate-200 pt-4 text-xs text-slate-500">This draft is informational and is not legal advice. The institution must review and approve the final notice, lawful bases, contact details, recipients, retention, and complaint process.</p>
</article>
